# SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
#
# Omarchy Mobile build of Mesa for the Pixel 7 Pro (Mali-G710 on Panthor)
# and the Pixel 6 and 6 Pro (Mali-G78 on Panfrost), plus Pixel 9a
# (Mali-G715 on Panthor).
#
# Derived from Arch Linux's mesa PKGBUILD, tag 1-26.2.4-1
# (https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/packaging/packages/mesa, 0BSD),
# which Arch Linux ARM also builds, with ALARM's documented differences
# (intel-rt off). Omarchy Mobile changes:
#  - 0001-panfrost-add-Mali-G710-to-the-model-table.patch (sent upstream,
#    see UPSTREAM.md); drop it once Mesa ships the entry.
#  - 0002-panfrost-don-t-make-image-BOs-private-on-panthor.patch: panthor
#    can't export a BO private to one GPU VM, and GTK 4 exports GL textures
#    created without PIPE_BIND_SHARED (GNOME Snapshot crashed after photos).
#  - 0003-panfrost-Advertise-Mali-G68-support.patch: upstream's 93d2c51f,
#    backported (drop it once Mesa ships it in a release).
#  - 0004-panfrost-add-Mali-G78-to-the-model-table.patch: the Pixel 6's
#    Mali-G78, next to the G68 (drop it once Mesa ships the G78 entry).
#  - aarch64 only, and only the drivers this phone can use: Gallium
#    panfrost (with kmsro), llvmpipe, softpipe and zink; Vulkan panfrost
#    (PanVK). Splits: mesa, vulkan-panfrost, vulkan-mesa-implicit-layers
#    (vulkan-panfrost depends on it). No rusticl, NVK, docs or valgrind,
#    so no Rust crates and a much shorter native build.
#  - 0005-0010: upstream G715 model and complete v11 support backports.
#    See README.md for pinned sources and validation limits.
#  - pkgrel 1.4: makepkg only allows integer[.integer], so the Omarchy Mobile
#    marker lives in the VERSION string (".omamobile4"), which shows up in
#    GL_VERSION and the libgallium file name.
#
# Maintainers of the original: Laurent Carlier, Felix Yan, Jan Alexander
# Steffens (heftig); contributors Jan de Groot, Andreas Radke.

pkgbase=mesa
pkgname=(
  mesa
  vulkan-panfrost
  vulkan-mesa-implicit-layers
)
pkgver=26.2.4
_pkgver=${pkgver/[a-z]/-&}
pkgrel=1.4
_omamobile=omamobile4
epoch=1
pkgdesc="Open-source OpenGL drivers (Omarchy Mobile: Mali-G710, Mali-G78, Mali-G715)"
url="https://www.mesa3d.org/"
arch=(aarch64)
license=("MIT AND BSD-3-Clause AND SGI-B-2.0")
